    <string name="bateria_dlg_instrucciones">The %1$s settings page will open. Go to “Battery” and choose “Unrestricted” (depending on your phone, it may be called “Don\'t optimize” or “Allow background activity”).</string>
    <string name="bateria_ahora_no">Not now</string>
    <string name="bateria_marca_intro">Besides removing Android\'s battery restriction, many manufacturers add their own power saving, which can close the app and stop alerts from arriving. Menu names vary by model and version.</string>
    <string name="bateria_marca_forzar">If you force-stop %1$s from the phone settings (“Force stop”), no alerts will arrive until you open it again.</string>
    <string name="bateria_marca_guia">Guide by brand (dontkillmyapp.com)</string>
    <string name="bateria_xiaomi">Settings → Apps → Manage apps → %1$s: turn on “Autostart” and, under “Battery saver”, choose “No restrictions”. Also, in the recent apps list, press and hold the %1$s card and tap the lock.</string>
    <string name="bateria_oppo">Settings → Apps → %1$s: allow “Auto-launch” and, in battery usage, “Allow background activity”.</string>
    <string name="bateria_samsung">Settings → Battery → Background usage limits: remove %1$s from the sleeping apps and add it to “Never sleeping apps”.</string>
    <string name="bateria_huawei">Settings → Apps → App launch → %1$s: turn off automatic management and turn on “Auto-launch”, “Secondary launch” and “Run in background”.</string>
    <string name="bateria_vivo">Settings → Battery → Background power consumption → %1$s: allow background activity and autostart.</string>
